{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan","id":486089,"title":"Which pop-culture Vampire belongs to which Clan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-20T00:59:36-07:00","id":486089,"title":"Which pop-culture Vampire belongs to which Clan","content":"Hallo everybody. I currently try to make the characteristics of the different Clans imaginable for newcomers. To do so I'm locking for examples of Vampires in movies, books and other media who match (at least roughly) one of the Clans. I am locking for several Examples, therefore I would be thankful for every suggestion.<br /> <br /> I think Daeva are pretty much Anne Rice, but what Vampire ells match them?<br /> <br /> Ventrue are Lord Ruthven and True Blood (because of Dominate and their constant trouble with their touchstones), but I think I missed something obvious.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu are Max Schreck and Murnau for sure, but are there examples of Nosferatu who are not ugly? Or ugly Nosferatu who are not funny but really terrifying?<br /> <br /> I thought Gangrel would be easy, but it isn't. Okay, Lost Boys and maybe From Dusk till Dawn, but did you ever saw Beast-like Vampires, who are or who are not transforming in to Animals, in a serious movie or book?<br /> <br /> Last one is the toughest I think. Which Vampires are Mekhet? Where did you saw the invisible? I think some of the many Vampire-Detectives could be a Mekhet, but which one is the most typical? Where did we saw a Vampire Cult? Which Vampire is such a stalker (no, not twilight Edward, yes he is a stalker, but he isn't good at it. I think twilight Vampires are Daeva, but that is a different story).<br /> <br /> Before you say Dracula, I have a Dracula-example for every Clan, because he shows characteristics of every. He is my example for a \u00dcber-Vampire.<br /> <br /> Thank you for ideas and suggestions.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. I'm locking for generalizations, so I prefer to say, the Vampire in this or that movie are like that specific Clan. I do not want to pick a specific Character if he is the only example in a given story and the other Vampires are much different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T02:47:37-07:00","id":486169,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen Let the Right One In but could that be a Mekhet? The thing with Mekhet is they don't get tv time because they don't do things wrong like the other clans do so humans don't like them.<br /> Mekhet are master clan! Let the lesser clans have their fame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T03:03:40-07:00","id":486178,"title":"","content":"A thousand nWoD fans are going to spit venom over this but... Edward Cullen would be a Nosferatu... Guy is creepy as hell!<br /> <br /> <br /> Fright Night would be good examples of Gangrel. They're wanderers, they sleep underground, and they were pretty bestial in how they attacked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-20-2015, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T03:33:26-07:00","id":486186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486169#post486169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen Let the Right One In but could that be a Mekhet? The thing with Mekhet is they don't get tv time because they don't do things wrong like the other clans do so humans don't like them.<br /> Mekhet are master clan! Let the lesser clans have their fame.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Let the Right One in, I'd say is a mix between a Mekhet and Daeva. (leaning more on the Mekhet)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T05:09:18-07:00","id":486237,"title":"","content":"No idea for a Mekhet, but I have the ideal example for a Gangrel, although you said not to mention him.<br /> <br /> Dracula from the book.<br /> His powers are:<br /> Controlling wolves, definitely Animalism<br /> Climbing on walls, can be achieved with protean<br /> Shape shifting into a wolf, bat, or dust/mist, is obviously protean<br /> Pretty hard to kill at night, sounds like Resilience to me<br /> Strong as several men, so he bought Vigor out of clan<br /> <br /> I don't think he showed any dominate-like powers in the book, but I'm only halfway through, and it's not hard to imagine him learning them out of clan. If there's anyone who represents the gangrel, it's Dracula.<br /> <br /> Plus, the masquerade gangrel clan was WW's first attempt at a Dracula clan, but they made their story so un-dracula like that they had to make the Tzimisce as a dracula clan (who also fit with his powers quite well if you switch vicissitude for protean).<br /> <br /> For a terrifying and ugly Nosferatu, you've suggested one, Count Orlok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T05:15:13-07:00","id":486252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486186#post486186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Let the Right One in, I'd say is a mix between a Mekhet and Daeva. (leaning more on the Mekhet)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funny, that was the first Film my mind came up with while thinking about Mekhet examples.<br /> <br /> Good start, keep on posting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T05:17:53-07:00","id":486254,"title":"","content":"Dio Brando strikes me as a pretty decent example of a Deva. He's fast, strong, and can charm people into doing pretty much anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T05:21:53-07:00","id":486257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486237#post486237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No idea for a Mekhet, but I have the ideal example for a Gangrel, although you said not to mention him.<br /> <br /> Dracula from the book.<br /> His powers are:<br /> Controlling wolves, definitely Animalism<br /> Climbing on walls, can be achieved with protean<br /> Shape shifting into a wolf, bat, or dust/mist, is obviously protean<br /> Pretty hard to kill at night, sounds like Resilience to me<br /> Strong as several men, so he bought Vigor out of clan<br /> <br /> I don't think he showed any dominate-like powers in the book, but I'm only halfway through, and it's not hard to imagine him learning them out of clan. If there's anyone who represents the gangrel, it's Dracula.<br /> <br /> Plus, the masquerade gangrel clan was WW's first attempt at a Dracula clan, but they made their story so un-dracula like that they had to make the Tzimisce as a dracula clan (who also fit with his powers quite well if you switch vicissitude for protean).<br /> <br /> For a terrifying and ugly Nosferatu, you've suggested one, Count Orlok.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you TwoD, but Dracula (yes, in the book) has aspects of every Clan, even Mekhet and Daeva. The Tzimisce btw. are more the WW-answer to the Wamphyri from the Necroscope series.<br /> <br /> Count Orloc in Nosferatu is Murnaus Dracula, played by the Actor Max Schreck, I mentioned that. But thank you, maybe you have another idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T05:25:19-07:00","id":486259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486254#post486254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dio Brando strikes me as a pretty decent example of a Deva. He's fast, strong, and can charm people into doing pretty much anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so in to Manga and Anime, but I will survey it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T06:54:39-07:00","id":486300,"title":"","content":"Eli from Let the Right One In strikes me as more of a Gangrel. Her vampiric, predatory nature seems to come across in more bestial, animalistic ways, especially in the book where she is described as being able to develop claws and membranes for flight. Not to mention her very matter-of-fact approach to her predation and the particularly brutal way she dispatches of Oskar's bullies at the end. <br /> <br /> As far as pop culture vampires that fit the Mekhet archetype, definitely Adam and Eve from Only Lovers Left Alive. They do not possess the usual super-strength, but are still very swift, very fast. They have refined senses, particularly Eve who has the power of psychometry (to know things about an object through touch alone). While they do not have powers akin to Obfuscate, the point stands that the both of them like to keep a fairly low profile and are fairly reclusive. The Mekhet-like obsession with knowledge is reflected in the obsessive nature of their hobbies; music and science for Adam, literature and the beauty of nature for Eve. Their interests in art and particularly Eve's interest in humanity would normally be seen as more of a Daeva trait, however they behave more like reluctant tourists of the human world. Witnesses, rather than participants. Detached and aloof. This strikes me as more of a 'Mekhet' way of acting as opposed to the balls-out hedonistic desperation for sensation and validation that marks the Daeva (Eve's 'sister' Ava is more of an impulsive, entitled Daeva with no sense of personal boundaries and endless appetite that is opposed to the ascetic tendencies of the two elder vampires).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5746-casper","name":"Casper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:05:34-07:00","id":486306,"title":"","content":"The vampires from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zXYO19Ig5hc\" target=\"_blank\"><i>30 Days of Night</i></a> seem like either Nosferatu or Gangrel: they're physically deformed and terrifying, but sprout claws and such. They display superhuman strength (and speed, but that's out-of-clan either way).<br /> <br /> I'd peg them as the best Nosferatu examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:12:12-07:00","id":486311,"title":"","content":"Despite the great liberties made with vampire lore in The Hunger, Miriam Blaylock strikes me as something of a more sophisticated variation on the Daeva. Outwardly cold and restrained, she is nevertheless so easily able to seduce Susan Sarandon's character and gain supernatural influence over her. Not only that, but she is absolutely terrified of loneliness, deceives her lovers to keep them with her only to ultimately discard them when they are no longer useful (although she will still keep them locked forever in her attic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5746-casper","name":"Casper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:31:01-07:00","id":486353,"title":"","content":"I have watched movies with vampires and was a little more specific. for example I was watching I think it was John Carpenter's vampires and the guy was super fast and super strong. So i figured he had Celerity and Vigor, which would likely make him a Daeva, or Perhaps a Nos.<br /> <br /> Cullen I think have Vigor and Celerity too which could easily make them Daeva or Nos too. He is super creepy and he makes people uncomfortable which could be his haunt, but also really popular which could effectively give him something like Awe.<br /> <br /> I think if anyone has read Anita Blake the clan's would be really great to go with there. Jean-Claude's Bloodline are definately Daeva. Where as the rotters ( i forget those guys' names ) are 100% Nos. There is a Padma who is the beast master and he would be a Gangrel. The clan that has the leader of Las Vegas would be Ventrue.<br /> <br /> The Vampires from Dusk til dawn ( tv and movie ) I think would be Gangrel since they shapeshift.<br /> <br /> I would agree that most of Anne Rice's Vampires would be Daeva.<br /> <br /> Blade would have a Mix of things. The council probably Ventrue. The second one most of them would Likely be Nos.<br /> <br /> Alucard from Helsing would likely be Gangrel with Protean and Dominate.<br /> <br /> Mehket are definitely harder to pinpoint, but you'd really have to look for specific abilities that would match the Disciplines.<br /> <br /> I totally agree that the 30days of Night vamps are Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> ( these are my opinions. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-20-2015, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:37:47-07:00","id":486355,"title":"","content":"Alucard from Hellsing is literally supposed to be Count Dracula, so...<br /> <br /> Although for what it's worth I too am in the &quot;Dracula was totes a Gangrel&quot; camp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:46:51-07:00","id":486360,"title":"","content":"From Fright Night, the Original, Jerry Dandrige strike me as either a ventrue or a gangrel. He make extensive use of Dominate (or possibly majesty) and has quite advanced protean.<br /> From the remake he seems to be mostly incredibly strong but somewhat creepy with very limited shapeshifting so maybe a nosferatu with just a tiny bit of protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T08:10:49-07:00","id":486412,"title":"","content":"Carmilla (from the novella and recent web series of the same name) seems a pretty clear example of a Daeva, albeit one with a few out-of-clan disciplines like Protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T08:21:12-07:00","id":486414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486355#post486355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alucard from Hellsing is literally supposed to be Count Dracula, so...<br /> <br /> Although for what it's worth I too am in the &quot;Dracula was totes a Gangrel&quot; camp.</div> </div> </div> </div>After all of the Beast spoilers, my headcanon is that Dracula was a vampire-like Beast. Probably Eshmaki with a Hunger for Prey.<br /> <br /> Anyway, on-topic, Alucard from <i>Castlevania: Symphony of the Night</i> is a Gangrel: Lots of shapeshifting (wolf, bat, mist). Handles his problems with physical violence rather than subtlety or social nuance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T08:39:44-07:00","id":486428,"title":"","content":"The film Byzantium has the best pop culture example of Mekhet in my opinion. Its a great vampire film that is often overlooked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantium_%28film%29\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8f/Poster_for_the_film_%22Byzantium%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantium_%28film%29\" target=\"_blank\"> Byzantium (film) - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantium_%28film%29\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantium_%28film%29 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The two main characters tend to exist on the fringes of society and act in large part as observers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","user":"Gravitas Man","date":". 04-20-2015, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T13:27:58-07:00","id":486668,"title":"","content":"vary interesting points. Byzantinum and only lovers... are on my list. Haven't saw them but I will. 30 days of night goes to the Gangrel imho. Not only because of the claws but because they are not Nosferatu. Sure, they are creepy, but the \u201clonely curse\u201d doesn\u2019t match with this huge pack of Vampires.<br /> <br /> Carmilla is actually a Daeva, she was mentioned in the Clanbook and in Dark Eras (I think it was there) as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T13:31:43-07:00","id":486686,"title":"","content":"Thomas Raith from the Dresden Files for Daeva. Along with Angel, Spike, and most popular vampires in current memory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T13:42:14-07:00","id":486700,"title":"","content":"Most of the vampires from the Dresden Files are Daeva, really. Well, the Red Court are in their human forms anyways- otherwise they're really nasty Nosferatu or Gangrel. Black Court vampires from the Dresden Files are probably Strix possessing corpses- at least, that's the closest I can figure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T14:30:26-07:00","id":486729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486428#post486428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The film Byzantium has the best pop culture example of Mekhet in my opinion. Its a great vampire film that is often overlooked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantium_%28film%29\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8f/Poster_for_the_film_%22Byzantium%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantium_%28film%29\" target=\"_blank\"> Byzantium (film) - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantium_%28film%29\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantium_%28film%29 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The two main characters tend to exist on the fringes of society and act in large part as observers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adore this movie. The island could make a great set piece for a weird Embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T15:41:04-07:00","id":486774,"title":"","content":"No one has brought up Buffy yet? For shame.<br /> <br /> Buffy vampires are in my opinion the perfect examples of Daeva. Most people go to Anne Rice, but they're much more like Toreador from Masquerade, with their vaguely psychic powers and their obsession with beautiful things (mostly beautiful people). While that is <i>an</i> aspect of Daeva, there's a lot more to them that I think Buffy captures exceptionally well. They're strong, they're fast, they're usually very pretty, and often use that to manipulate people, so they've got the Discipline spread down. Theyre all debauched as hell and love being evil just because it's fun, so that covers their 1e Clan weakness. Both of the major male vampire characters eventually fall in love with Buffy, and there are multiple other examples of vampires developing unhealthy obsessions with human characters, so there's the 2e Clan Bane.<br /> <br /> Most importantly to me though, they're all extremely passionate, and that passion expresses itself in a variety of ways for different characters. Angel is your classic broody heartthrob. Drusilla gets the sexy-but-crazy angle. Spike embodies aggression, and thrill-seeking, with a healthy dose of massochism. Though he ultimately is, in his own words, &quot;love's bitch, but at least I'm man enough to admit it&quot;. Even the minor vampire characters, on the occasions that we get the chance to delve a bit into their motivations, are entirely driven by passion, and all have different takes on it.<br /> <br /> The Master and the Turok-Han (and I've always kind of thought The Master was one of them) are the exception, but they're clearly Nosferatu - they've all got the classic Count Orloch face, they all live underground (technically inside the hellmouth, but come on), they're super strong, their presence has a terrifying and divisive influence on Buffy and the potentials... We don't see any examples of them using Obfuscate, but then, that's exactly how Obfuscate works, and they <i>did</i> pretty much show up out of nowhere near the end of the final season (unless you count The Master, and <i>he</i> was only in the first season and that one random alternate timeline episode.)<br /> <br /> ...I really like Buffy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T15:48:42-07:00","id":486781,"title":"","content":"Well in the Buffyverse vamps get uglier with age, so they all start deva and end up nosferatu if they live long enough. <br /> <br /> Also as demons piloting a soulless corpse they also have a fair bit in common with the Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T16:00:28-07:00","id":486788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486781#post486781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well in the Buffyverse vamps get uglier with age, so they all start deva and end up nosferatu if they live long enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Get out of here with your not-mentioned-in-the-actual-show lore!<br /> <br /> (I am of course being playful and actually have nothing against the EU, I just loved the show, and everything I've heard about the comics and such has sounded very strange to me)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486781#post486781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also as demons piloting a soulless corpse they also have a fair bit in common with the Strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad I'm not the only one who saw that parallel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-20-2015, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T02:18:05-07:00","id":487120,"title":"","content":"Another decent Vampire film, Near Dark. Pretty spot on interpretation of Gangrel. A family of nomadic and aggressive vampires.<br /> <br /> This scene captures the tone of the film pretty well. It's a bit dated in places but it holds up well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7RR-nVtxvlI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7RR-nVtxvlI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7RR-nVtxvlI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7RR-nVtxvlI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T06:56:59-07:00","id":487225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486353#post486353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alucard from Helsing would likely be Gangrel with Protean and Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Pijavica","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T07:32:03-07:00","id":487260,"title":"","content":"I suppose Nick and Cym from <i>The</i> <i>Forsaken </i>would be Ventrue nomads with a high tendency to create revenants. The Night Flyer a Nosferatu, though I'm basing this on the movie. Richard Laymon makes some of my favorite vampires, if they're vampires at all. <i>The Traveling Vampire Show</i> probably shows Gangrel, while <i>Bite </i>depicts a Daeva, and <i>The Stake</i> a Mekhet, <i>In The Dark</i> depicts a particularly ugly Mekhet or Nosferatu. Edward Lee's <i>Brides of the Impaler</i> some Lancea et Sanctum Nosferatu, likely part of a heretic caste. I try to imagine Edimmu like the vampires from <i>Lifeforce</i>. Charlee Jacob's vampires are probably Nosferatu sired by some unimaginably powerful elder with a vicious curse and some spirit guides.<br /> <br /> <i>Innocent Blood</i> might fit the more vice-oriented first edition Daeva. The <i>Vampire Boys</i> series and <i>Vampire Killers</i> movies depict Daeva, though with the former I think Demetrius might have been a Gangrel. With the latter it's possible they were Mekhet. They certainly belonged to the Circle of the Crone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Reconsidered the Brides 04-21-2015, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T02:07:10-07:00","id":488086,"title":"","content":"Wow, thank you nofather, that was comprehensive!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T05:33:33-07:00","id":488182,"title":"","content":"No problem. There's also the book <i>Draculas</i>, by Jack Kilborn and Blake Crouch. It sort of takes the 'fast zombie' concept to vampires, with people being transformed in the course of seconds by mere drops of saliva. The end result would, in game terms, be frenzied 0 Humanity Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-mIPBD6cB8Yk/Twtb49YkizI/AAAAAAAAAgc/ZUwvg0n5QD8/s1600/Screen%2Bshot%2B2012-01-09%2Bat%2B1.48.46%2BPM.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-22-2015, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T05:34:17-07:00","id":488183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486788#post486788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get out of here with your not-mentioned-in-the-actual-show lore!</div> </div> </div> </div>It was mentionned in the show though, In the first season of Angel, episode 7, Darla mention the fact that the master has grow beyond the curse of mortal features.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, a lot of modern day vampires are Daeva while older ones includes characteristics of all the clans.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T08:38:42-07:00","id":488294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486428#post486428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The film Byzantium has the best pop culture example of Mekhet in my opinion. Its a great vampire film that is often overlooked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantium_%28film%29\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8f/Poster_for_the_film_%22Byzantium%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantium_%28film%29\" target=\"_blank\"> Byzantium (film) - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantium_%28film%29\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantium_%28film%29 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The two main characters tend to exist on the fringes of society and act in large part as observers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Order are, but I'd rate the main two as Nosferatu. While they <i>can</i> reel people in, it tends to be people who are lonelycursed themselves in some way - both of them always seem a bit off unless they really try.<br /> <br /> Thanks for bringing the film up, by the way. Brilliant film.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T08:59:22-07:00","id":488354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=488183#post488183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was mentionned in the show though, In the first season of Angel, episode 7, Darla mention the fact that the master has grow beyond the curse of mortal features</div> </div> </div> </div>Angel and Buffy are not the same show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T09:30:40-07:00","id":488371,"title":"","content":"Elderand might have meant Buffy, since Darla wasn't in the seventh episode of the first season of Angel.<br /> <br /> Also, the Turok-Han Vampires were pretty ugly. I'd probably have made them the first Nosferatu, the ones from the deeps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T09:57:39-07:00","id":488392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=488354#post488354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angel and Buffy are not the same show.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kakistos is said to be &quot;so old his hands and feet are cloven&quot; and what we see of him is fairly monstrous all around; he doesn't seem to have a human guise anymore&gt;, he's all-vampface all the time.<br /> <br /> And yes, Darla said that in the 7th episode of <i>Buffy</i>, not <i>Angel</i>.<br /> <br /> So, unless you want to get <i>super</i> nitpicky, it <i>has</i> been mentioned in the show. Also, it's really nitpicky to say that they aren't the same show when they exist in the same universe, so one show's lore is necessarily the other show's lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T10:03:53-07:00","id":488416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=488392#post488392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kakistos is said to be &quot;so old his hands and feet are cloven&quot; and what we see of him is fairly monstrous all around; he doesn't seem to have a human guise anymore&gt;, he's all-vampface all the time.<br /> <br /> And yes, Darla said that in the 7th episode of <i>Buffy</i>, not <i>Angel</i>.<br /> <br /> So, unless you want to get <i>super</i> nitpicky, it <i>has</i> been mentioned in the show. Also, it's really nitpicky to say that they aren't the same show when they exist in the same universe, so one show's lore is necessarily the other show's lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... You're right, I guess I just didn't pick up on those passing mentions. My mistake there.<br /> <br /> It's not that nitpicky to call Buffy and Angel different shows though, considering they had different show runners, different writing teams, and were on different networks. Yes, they are part of the same fictional universe, but with the drastically different tone and writing style, I have known many Buffy fans who never watched Angel and a few Angel fans who never watched Buffy. Spinoff =/= same show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T10:20:30-07:00","id":488429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=488416#post488416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm... You're right, I guess I just didn't pick up on those passing mentions. My mistake there.<br /> <br /> It's not that nitpicky to call Buffy and Angel different shows though, considering they had different show runners, different writing teams, and were on different networks. Yes, they are part of the same fictional universe, but with the drastically different tone and writing style, I have known many Buffy fans who never watched Angel and a few Angel fans who never watched Buffy. Spinoff =/= same show.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing my point, which I probably didn't make well-enough: them not being the same show is a bad reason for not taking one show's lore as acceptable with regards to its sister show, because they co-exist in the same universe, per canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T10:40:01-07:00","id":488467,"title":"","content":"Actually I didn't get the show wrong, I did however get the season wrong. 7th episode of Angel second season: Darla.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T10:48:20-07:00","id":488475,"title":"","content":"The lore is the same in both Buffy and Angel. So if vampire lore was true in Buffy it will be true in Angel. But this thread is waaaayyyy off topic.<br /> <br /> Remember that Nos just could potentially run in packs (30 days of Night) Because it specifically says that the lonely curse does not apply to Kindred and touchstones. Only interactions with Humans. <br /> <br /> Nos can also be extremely beautiful so much so it makes people uncomfortable. We would have to look at what they do and less what they look like. Super strong or just randomly disappear (vigor and Obfuscate ) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T10:52:09-07:00","id":488477,"title":"","content":"I really saw the 30 Days of Night vampires as more Gangrel, they were very bestial and seemed in touch with their Beasts, just riding the wave the entire time.<br /> <br /> In the comic, they were sort of looked down upon by other, more superior vampires, who were annoyed that these guys were going to break the Masquerade. The other vampires might be more appropriate as Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T11:29:40-07:00","id":488535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=488429#post488429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're missing my point, which I probably didn't make well-enough: them not being the same show is a bad reason for not taking one show's lore as acceptable with regards to its sister show, because they co-exist in the same universe, per canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said I don't accept Angel's lore as canon. I was merely unaware of Angel's lore because it's a different show that I did not watch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T14:08:58-07:00","id":488672,"title":"","content":"Okay, we had some interesting suggestions. Can we go a level higher and start to argue why a specific version of Vampire are this or that clan?<br /> <br /> I am relay confused with 30 Days... Gangrel or Nosferatu for sure. Sure, Nosferatu do not have to be lonely, but I think they should be rather cold, not such emotional. The Vampires in 30 Days are terrifying because of they beast-like behavior, they lash out the Beast all the time rather than using Nightmare. So I stay with Gangrel. Is ther any example for a Vampire using Nightmare btw.?<br /> <br /> Now for Buffy. When I was young I hated the show. Now I understand what is interesting on Buffy, but I do not have the time to watch the whole series. But I want to be sure about the Buffy Vampires because the Show was so popular. I think it is common sense, that the Turok-Han are pretty much Nosferatu. What is with the standard Buffy-Vampires? Which powers, which demeanor, which curse do they show?<br /> <br /> True Blood, and Polidors Vampyr are pretty Ventrue-like Vampires. But is there any classic aristocratic Vampire whith dominate powers beside Dracula?<br /> <br /> The Daeva seems to get the most examples. Not shure if we need more.<br /> <br /> Mekhet are still a problem. I'm still not satisfied with the few Mekhet examples. We have to find some more. What we are looking for is a rather silent type of Vampire. Rather quick then strong. Mysterious and may be invisible or super silence, with a kind of Telepathic / supersense Power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T14:50:14-07:00","id":488731,"title":"","content":"The vampires from <i>Penny Dreadful</i> may be Mekhet. They have a strong tie to Egypt, to the point that there's hieroglyphs carved into their skeletons. There may be some mind control there as well. They can send dreams, I believe.<br /> <br /> In my previously mentioned <i>In The Dark</i>, <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">the vampire is incredibly smart, inhumanly sneaky, very fast and agile. It's also very aware of things going on where it shouldn't be able to know what's going on.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-22-2015, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T15:35:54-07:00","id":488789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=488672#post488672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now for Buffy. When I was young I hated the show. Now I understand what is interesting on Buffy, but I do not have the time to watch the whole series. But I want to be sure about the Buffy Vampires because the Show was so popular. I think it is common sense, that the Turok-Han are pretty much Nosferatu. What is with the standard Buffy-Vampires? Which powers, which demeanor, which curse do they show?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Buffy, vampires are corpses that have been posessed by demons. They are explicitly stated to have no soul, the soul having been replaced by the demon. However, the vampire's personallity seems to be heavily influenced by that of the person they were in life, but twisted into something much darker. They seem to enjoy doing evil for its own sake, and are presumably incapable of feeling empathy. There are two examples (that I know of) of vampires who regain their souls, one due to a curse and another as a &quot;reward&quot; for completing a series of ritualistic trials. In both cases, they retained their vampiric abilities, but we're driven mad as the guilt of all of the sins they had committed in the absence of their soul hit them all at once.<br /> <br /> As for powers, they are of course immortal. They are not impervious to harm, but heal very quickly and can only be killed by removing the head, a wooden stake to the heart, or sunlight or fire, all of which turn them to ash. They seem to be able to withstand low levels of sunlight for short periods. They are also superhumanly strong and fast, though not the near-teleportation levels of speed seen in some other sources. Dracula shows up in one episode and can turn into a bat, or into mist, and displays Dominate-like mind control, but according to Spike (one of the main vampire characters), he's somehow cheating, showing off with Magic that is not inherent to being a vampire (of course, Dracula claims orherwise, so take that as you will).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T15:46:05-07:00","id":488798,"title":"","content":"<i>Ultraviolet</i>'s (Channel 4, not the film) are ambiguous. That's mostly because they're shown from the limited perspective of their hunters. They can kick arse in person when they need to, but they prefer a hands off approach often managing conspiracies. They better represent Invictus and Ordo Dracul together than any clan. They're susceptible to the traditional banes, they don't leave fingerprints, reflections or voice transmissions. They don't seem to have mind control powers, anything to do with animals or physical deformities, unless they been in the sun which doesn't heal. They might fit Mekhet or Ventrue to a lesser extent.<br /> <br /> One point I clean forgot. If they know that you know what they are and they want to talk to you, they might just show up in your room. The young ones at least. It isn't explained how they do that. When you think about what Mekhet can do, it must be near indistinguishable from teleportation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 04-22-2015, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T16:35:12-07:00","id":488821,"title":"","content":"Penny Dreadful, I knew I missed something. I'm not sure how to handle Penny Dreadful. Everything you (nofather) said is true, but they are related to Dracula again. I will meditate about that, but good point.<br /> <br /> I know the basic concept of Buffy-Vampires, but can you brake it down to a archetype?<br /> I mean, you know, every Requiem Clan is a kind of archetypical Vampire.<br /> Daeva are the seducer, succubus Vamps.<br /> Ventrue are the aristocratic Vampire Lords.<br /> Nosferatu are sheer monstrous Vampire-Creatures.<br /> Gangrel are the animal like Vampire-Beasts.<br /> And Mekhet are the mysterious and silent Vampire-Stranger.<br /> <br /> Which one did you think fits best to Buffy/ Angelo-Vampires?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile I will check out Ultraviolet <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","user":"Sethos","date":". 04-22-2015, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T16:39:20-07:00","id":488828,"title":"","content":"I think different Buffy vampires fit into different clans, they all sort of hit the archetypes as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T16:47:49-07:00","id":488835,"title":"","content":"Hm, than they are pretty useless for my idea to illustrate the Clans. It's the same with the Blade-Vampires, who are pretty much VtM-Vampires. The pack in Blade 2 is even called the \u201cpack\u201d, with a \u201cPriest\u201d, who looks like an old Clan Tzimisce, some Lasombra, Brucah-Antitribu and an Assamite-Antitribu as well. Pretty obvious, but that is another story. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T16:58:36-07:00","id":488843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=488821#post488821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the basic concept of Buffy-Vampires, but can you brake it down to a archetype?<br /> I mean, you know, every Requiem Clan is a kind of archetypical Vampire.<br /> Daeva are the seducer, succubus Vamps.<br /> Ventrue are the aristocratic Vampire Lords.<br /> Nosferatu are sheer monstrous Vampire-Creatures.<br /> Gangrel are the animal like Vampire-Beasts.<br /> And Mekhet are the mysterious and silent Vampire-Stranger.<br /> <br /> Which one did you think fits best to Buffy/ Angelo-Vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're pretty distinctly Daeva, for the reasons I gave in my earlier post in which I first brought them up: they clearly have Vigor and Celerity, and could be argued to have Majesty. They are all debauched and love doing bad stuff because it's fun, and they often develop unhealthy obsessions with humans, which covers the Daeva's 1e Weakness and 2e Bane, respectively. Most importantly, they are driven almost entirely by their passions, which to me is much more what Daeva are about than merely being seductive. Although, as was mentioned, they do grow more monstrous with age, making the oldest ones pretty Nos-like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:05:40-07:00","id":488847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=488843#post488843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they're pretty distinctly Daeva, for the reasons I gave in my earlier post in which I first brought them up: they clearly have Vigor and Celerity, and could be argued to have Majesty. They are all debauched and love doing bad stuff because it's fun, and they often develop unhealthy obsessions with humans, which covers the Daeva's 1e Weakness and 2e Bane, respectively. Most importantly, they are driven almost entirely by their passions, which to me is much more what Daeva are about than merely being seductive. Although, as was mentioned, they do grow more monstrous with age, making the oldest ones pretty Nos-like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, if no one disagree, I put Buffy on the Daeva side. The point, that they become ugly by aging could be true in a way for every Vampire. Or is it a spontaneous change (like they loose humanity and the lonely-Curs switch on, you know?!)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T19:09:09-07:00","id":488955,"title":"","content":"In comics, there was also an Elseworlds story where Batman faced Dracula, but not 'the' Dracula, and became a vampire. A particularly melodramatic one. But he was Gangrel all the way. In addition to showing signs of Animalism, through summoning and controlling bats, Protean, where he grew wings and shifted his body, as well as sank into the soil and turned into a dark mist. There was even Resilience.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i100.photobucket.com/albums/m27/victoria_wayne/c_arena/countdownarena_01_04.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T06:12:04-07:00","id":489411,"title":"","content":"Also, all Buffy vamps rise from the dead knowing kung-fu (I can't remember the episode but I swear she mentioned it once).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T09:06:44-07:00","id":489560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=488821#post488821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Penny Dreadful, I knew I missed something. I'm not sure how to handle Penny Dreadful. Everything you (nofather) said is true, but they are related to Dracula again. I will meditate about that, but good point.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Meanwhile I will check out Ultraviolet <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'd rate Buffyverse vampires as Strix rather than any clan. They're innately evil combinations of a dead body and possessing monster spirit.<br /> <br /> Regarding Penny Dreadful, I'm pretty sure &quot;the Master&quot; goes well beyond Dracula. I think I'd go with a Nosferatu bloodline whose unique Discipline is the granting of extra vampiric power to ghouls (Mina and the other pale girl vamps are actually ghouls on which this Discipline's been used).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T11:07:32-07:00","id":489658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486774#post486774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Master and the Turok-Han (and I've always kind of thought The Master was one of them) are the exception, but they're clearly Nosferatu - they've all got the classic Count Orloch face, they all live underground (technically inside the hellmouth, but come on), they're super strong, their presence has a terrifying and divisive influence on Buffy and the potentials... We don't see any examples of them using Obfuscate, but then, that's exactly how Obfuscate works, and they <i>did</i> pretty much show up out of nowhere near the end of the final season (unless you count The Master, and <i>he</i> was only in the first season and that one random alternate timeline episode.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In &quot;Prophecy Girl&quot; the Master plays cat-and-mouse with Buffy, hiding in shadows and behind pillars before getting the drop on her from behind. I'd say he has Obfuscate, though not at a high level (spent his XP on developing Blood Sorcery instead, I'm guessing).<br /> <br /> Mr. Barlow and his progeny in Salem's Lot would be good examples of the Nosferatu. Him with the classic appearance, the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vV1V0U41HI4\" target=\"_blank\">newbies like Danny Glick by being creeptastic in general</a>.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T11:28:22-07:00","id":489676,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem with basing clan just on power is that vampires can get the clan disciplines of other clans, and for vampires that have been around for hundreds of years it's probably not even uncommon for them to have the clan-specific discipline of at least two other clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T11:38:58-07:00","id":489706,"title":"","content":"Generally in a given fiction vampires all have the same power set though, so it's as if only one clan exists in that 'verse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T11:42:18-07:00","id":489707,"title":"","content":"It depends on the fiction. In something like the Buffyverse, you have a ton of vampires with a variety of powers. Dracula could turn to mist, Master could obfuscate, use the equivalent of dominate, and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-23-2015, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T11:56:09-07:00","id":489718,"title":"","content":"Let's see . . .<br /> <br /> ~ The vampires in From Dusk Till Dawn (the original) I'd call Gangrel, in the Mabry bloodline, considering the way the bar / temple is used to lure victims in off of the road (plus the monstrous shape shifting and the trained giant snakes in the dancers' routines). Granted, they're a little . . . squishy . . . so maybe they're a bit low on Resilience.<br /> <br /> ~ The ones featured in Laurell Hamilton's &quot;Anita Blake&quot; series I'd consider Daeva; they're portrayed as sexy, fast, and strong. I suppose the same could also apply to Kim Harrison's &quot;Hollows&quot; series vampires as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T18:05:32-07:00","id":655750,"title":"","content":"If I may resurrect the thread...<br /> <br /> Are any of you guys watching <i>The Strain</i>? If so, what do you think of this show's vampires: Nosferatu? Gangrel? Admittedly, most of them would qualify only as larvae...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T19:15:41-07:00","id":655811,"title":"","content":"With the strange mental stuff I'd actually say a mix of mekhet <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/\" target=\"_blank\">neglatu</a> and revenants. Certainly they're ugly, and bestial, but I think their shadowy manipulation, psychic powers and overall cunning plan fits more with mekhet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:21:36-07:00","id":657249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486686#post486686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thomas Raith from the Dresden Files for Daeva. Along with Angel, Spike, and most popular vampires in current memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>My friends and I went through Buffy back during Masquerade. Angel's Ventrue, Spike's Toreador,(Daeva) and Drusilla's Malkavian.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T20:03:14-07:00","id":657309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=657249#post657249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My friends and I went through Buffy back during Masquerade. Angel's Ventrue, Spike's Toreador,(Daeva) and Drusilla's Malkavian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Angel sired Drusilla, who sired Spike, so they'd all be the same Clan. I really think all three are Daeva.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T03:09:56-07:00","id":657579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=655750#post655750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may resurrect the thread...<br /> <br /> Are any of you guys watching <i>The Strain</i>? If so, what do you think of this show's vampires: Nosferatu? Gangrel? Admittedly, most of them would qualify only as larvae...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be a little quirky, I would say they are Pijavica or Cymothoa Sanguinaria (from Wicked Dead). But as long as we use just the standard rules, what would I recommend if a player likes to play that kind of Vampire? Not easy. I think Nosferatu is a natural choice, because the transformation goes along with several physical changes (which do not make them nicer). The second thing is, that The Strain-Vampires have some psycic-powers which a Gangrel hardly have. A Nosferatu with Nightmare (since 2nd edition) could do such effects. Maybe I would make this type of Vampires a Nosferatu Bloodline, with Protean and an affinity to leeches, for things like the tongue and other physical ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T03:27:15-07:00","id":657584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=657309#post657309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that Angel sired Drusilla, who sired Spike, so they'd all be the same Clan. I really think all three are Daeva.</div> </div> </div> </div>True - Daeva covers pretty nicely the whole spectre of variety in the Master's descendants in a way that would be complicated with the Masquerade ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T04:10:53-07:00","id":657630,"title":"","content":"As far as Dresden Files vamps go The White Court are a mixture of Daeva and Nosferatu, depending on what they feed on, Black Court are Ventrue who look like Strix-possessed corpses, and I'm not sure what the red court would be. Probably Daeva again, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T07:57:30-07:00","id":657889,"title":"","content":"Weren't those the bat-like things? I'd say Gangrel that can't turn off their Aspects but can hide inside a human skin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T08:11:33-07:00","id":657897,"title":"","content":"They're actually closest to he Bonsam from VtM Dark Ages. One that has the fifth dot of their unique discipline automatically, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T09:55:04-07:00","id":658047,"title":"","content":"The Dresden Files Vampires are special, because they just have something like Clans, and everyone is a very special kind of creature, sometimes every Court is very heterogeneous too. So you can hardly say, this Clan or this Clan is like the Dresden File Vampires. But You can use the series to illustrate Clan or covenant interaction. If you use Wicked Dead, Dresden Files are a great reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T04:50:06-07:00","id":662969,"title":"","content":"Nosferatu are very rare, as Requim Nos are basically Boogeymen, and powerwise have more in common with with creatures like IT than most vampires.<br /> <br /> Really most ugly vamps are more like ugly Gangrel than Nos. Gangrel pretty much cover all the feral beasts versions of vamps, like 30 Days of Night. Basically, if the plot of the movie would only be slightly changed by switching out vamps with werewolves, its a Gangrel.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T17:19:19-07:00","id":663570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=662969#post662969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nosferatu are very rare, as Requim Nos are basically Boogeymen, and powerwise have more in common with with creatures like IT than most vampires.<br /> <br /> Really most ugly vamps are more like ugly Gangrel than Nos. Gangrel pretty much cover all the feral beasts versions of vamps, like 30 Days of Night. Basically, if the plot of the movie would only be slightly changed by switching out vamps with werewolves, its a Gangrel.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes of coarse, if it behave like an animal, it is mostly a Kind of Gangrel. But remember, that every Vampire has a beast in his soul. The Werewolf-Gangrel analogy sounds like a good indicator.<br /> <br /> Did you have more examples for this type of Vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T17:36:25-07:00","id":663605,"title":"","content":"I saw Underworld recently and think about, which clan this type could be.<br /> <br /> They seem to have more or less no psychic abilities. They seem to be very pathetic, so I think they are rather not one of the coldblooded Ventrue. On the other hand, they have nearly no relationship to humans, so they could still be Ventrues.<br /> <br /> The Same with Nosferatu. They are not as ugly, but we know, Nosferatu are not necessary ugly, but creepy. Yes, I think they are creepy. Could be.<br /> <br /> The lack of human relationship make it hard to believe, that they could be Daeva. But they are physically superior, so we maybe do not see the relationships in the movies.<br /> <br /> Gangrel, well they do not often change shape, but the old an mighty one could. Thay are still though, so maybe they are Gangrel.<br /> <br /> Last but not least Mekhet. Interesting: strange cult, communication via blood rituals, rather subtle powers, intriguer... I think, I would go with Mekhet. What did you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T18:10:14-07:00","id":663639,"title":"","content":"I always thought they were Ventrue. But Masquerade Ventrue. Just without explicit use of Dominate, I think.<br /> <br /> There was a <a href=\"http://boards.straightdope.com/sdmb/showthread.php?t=209962\" target=\"_blank\">lawsuit</a> against the production of the films, for taking things from World of Darkness to make the movies.<br /> <br /> As an interesting side note he later went on to write I, Frankenstein.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-13-2015, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T05:31:57-07:00","id":664135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=663639#post663639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought they were Ventrue. But Masquerade Ventrue. Just without explicit use of Dominate, I think.<br /> <br /> There was a <a href=\"http://boards.straightdope.com/sdmb/showthread.php?t=209962\" target=\"_blank\">lawsuit</a> against the production of the films, for taking things from World of Darkness to make the movies.<br /> <br /> As an interesting side note he later went on to write I, Frankenstein.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes I know. I saw the first Movie with my at that time Masquerade-group and we knew, it was a WoD-rip-off. I think the different houses which were mentioned in the movie should be different clans, but we never saw enough of them to know if they have different flaws and merits depending on the house.<br /> But the idea of this tread was to illustrate Requem by Pop-Culture Vampires. So If someone says, he want to play a Vampire like that one in Underworld, which clan should be recommended?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T05:52:37-07:00","id":664147,"title":"","content":"As far as I recall, there's no real distinction between the Houses in Underworld. Certainly none that really stood out. You could make an argument that they stole the torpor idea, but really all the other stuff is just basic Vampire tropes. And the werewolves don't bear much resemblance to the Garou at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T06:45:45-07:00","id":664241,"title":"","content":"I always thought the idea of <i>Underworld</i> stealing from the World of Darkness to be kind of silly. Most of the things that were complaints were things like, &quot;they sleep for a long time!&quot; and &quot;vampires and werewolves hate each other!&quot; Neither of which were particularly new even when the classic WoD was first published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T08:37:57-07:00","id":664344,"title":"","content":"Yeah, White Wolf complaining is a bit like Starcraft or Warcraft complaining. All three games basically stole decades of tropes and codified them into a game. They invented very few truly new ideas, except the idea of mashing old ideas into one game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T09:10:59-07:00","id":664446,"title":"","content":"It was close enough for With Wolf to take action against the production and close enough for Lakeshore Entertainment to find a settlement with WW instead of stay the court proceeding to the end.<br /> <br /> But can we pleas stay in topic? Which Clan? After a long time of thinking I tend to non-ugly Nosferatu, or rather irascible Mekhet. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T09:22:54-07:00","id":664462,"title":"","content":"They have a strictly hierarchical aristocratic society with lots of politicking, so Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T09:26:32-07:00","id":664466,"title":"","content":"Yeah, just Ventrue without dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T09:32:04-07:00","id":664470,"title":"","content":"Or Animalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T09:37:06-07:00","id":664475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=664462#post664462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have a strictly hierarchical aristocratic society with lots of politicking, so Ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Invictus Daeva don't politic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T09:56:34-07:00","id":664510,"title":"","content":"I understand, why Ventrue seem so obvious, but to be honest, hierarchical and aristocratic, are rather social traits. So I think they behavior is more or less an indicator for they covenant. So I would say they are Invictus for sure. But Invictus of which clan?<br /> <br /> The Underworld-Vampires do not seem so aristocratic to me (For the exception of respect the age, but that is more or less a Blood Potency thing). They are rather pathetic and emotional unstable, what didn't sound like the coldblooded Ventrue. They often appear and disappear out of or in to nowhere, so I think obfuscate or celerity is working hear. So Nosferatu, Daeva and Mekhet are possible.<br /> They seem to have rather no relationship to humans in general, what could be an indication for Ventrue, but exclude Daeva. So Nosferatu and Mekhet are still in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T10:00:41-07:00","id":664516,"title":"","content":"The age thing has a bit of a quirk, actually, because the first vampire and the oldest vampire aren't the same guy. The first went and sired an old man while he was still within the range of a mortal lifespan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T10:05:56-07:00","id":664520,"title":"","content":"I still say Ventrue. They don't seem the slightest bit interested in fear and most aren't hideous, they don't particularly lean towards secrets or information or shadows. Instead they are a thin veneer of self control and civility over monstrous control-freaks. I think you could say Selene is a daeva, as she's clearly led by her passions, and maybe the fop whose name I forget who had a crush on her, but the others are pretty clearly Ventrue, who are led by their arrogance and self-centeredness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-14-2015, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T10:10:40-07:00","id":664522,"title":"","content":"Passionate Ventrue are allowed, y'know. The Daeva don't have a patent or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T10:14:23-07:00","id":664526,"title":"","content":"That's true but she's ruled by them. She's hung out with a guy for all of ten minutes before she's ready to throw her entire immortal life away for him, all her loyalties and everything she's built.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T10:56:19-07:00","id":664549,"title":"","content":"I am not satisfied with the way this went. It seems (and other said that before but I couldn\u2019t heed on them. Stupid sethos!) that the Underworld-Vampires are to generic to fit proper into one Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T11:55:20-07:00","id":664579,"title":"","content":"It might be hard to assign a clan, but covenant-wise, they're pretty firm Invictus. (The werewolves are more like the Ordo Dracul than anything; which is where I reiterate my occasional observation that I wish they'd gone with the idea, which I read somewhere was the initial plan, of two breeds of werewolf rather than werewolves and vampires).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T12:31:06-07:00","id":664643,"title":"","content":"I'm going to try <i>Elder Scrolls</i> vampires.<br /> <br /> <u>Arena</u><br /> They're badarse spellcasters who wear cloaks. Not enough information<br /> <br /> <u>Daggerfall</u><br /> They look and sound weird, which would suggest <b>Nosferatu</b>, but nobody seems to notice that in game. In fact, one of them writes a book about his experiences and describes what it was like meeting a friend from life. He had been buried and everyone thought he was dead. Nobody recognised him, but he was treated much like a human stranger.<br /> There are nine &quot;tribes&quot;. All that distinguishes them is which cut cost spells they get. So I'll list them and make stuff up about them if needs be:<br /> <br /> Vraseth - &quot;Nimbleness&quot; - I think these guy as the types who scuttle around dungeons and trees and move unpredictably like Voldo from <i>Soul Calibur </i>or Jack from <i>Power Stone. </i>Apparently, the younger Queen Dowager thought that one of their castles would be a safe place to keep her private documents. That would fit a <b>Nosferatu</b> archetype nicely. That sort physical ability may otherwise match <b>Gangrel </b>or <b>Daeva</b>.<br /> <br /> Haarvenu - Big flashy fire and ice spells -These abilities wouldn't directly help them hunt, but they may be used to inspire awe and fear from mortal herds. I think of them setting up blood cults in rural western High Rock. <b>Daeva </b>or<b> Ventrue</b>?<br /> <br /> Garlythi - Shield - That's like fortitude so possibly <b>Gangrel </b>or<b> Ventrue</b>.<br /> <br /> Thrafey - Heal - A bit like the above. They're coded as enemies of the Anthosis. Perhaps they're a new tribe with a new ability so the Anthosis abduct them for study when they can. I'm going with <b>Gangrel</b>.<br /> <br /> Lyrezi - Silence and Invisibility - Probably <b>Mekhet</b>, but maybe <b>Nosferatu</b>.<br /> <br /> Khulari - Paralysis - Well certainly not Daeva. Could be <b>Mekhet, Nosferatu </b>or <b>Gangrel</b>.<br /> <br /> Montalion - Free action (cures paralysis) - The ability is worthless for two reasons and I've got nothing.<br /> <br /> Anthosis - They don't get a spell. They get a constant intelligence boost. I'd say <b>Mehket </b>or even <b>Jiang Shi</b><i>.</i><br /> <br /> Selenu - Resist fire, cold or shock. Better at withstanding the elements? How about <b>Gangrel</b>?<br /> <br /> <u>Morrowind</u><br /> As well as looking and sounding weird, everyone see that they're vampires in the mechanics, which means that you can hardly speak to anyone and everybody shouts at you or pleads for his life. They stay tombs and ruins. That's as <b>Nosferatu</b> as most vampires get in TES<i>. </i>There are three clans:<br /> <br /> Aundae - High Elves with enhanced willpower and magical ability. They also dress much more smartly than the other clans. They hypnotise their prey. <b>Ventrue</b>.<br /> Berne - Cyrodiils who pride themselves being able to go everywhere unseen. That's quite <b>Mekhet</b>.<br /> Quarra - Really strong Nords who run at their prey, grab and bite and probably spill a lot of the blood. Other clan think they're wasteful, ugly brutes and they think the other clans are pathetically weak, especially Aundae. <b>Gangrel</b><br /> <br /> <u>Oblivion</u><br /> They pass as mortals and rely on influence over mortal society. That's Invictus. I'd say <b>Ventrue</b>, based on the tone of their manifesto.<br /> <br /> <u>Skyrim</u><br /> Largely a rip off of <i>Oblvion's</i> vampires, but they can raise corpses and are more distant from mortal society. Some of them seem quite keen on eating flesh. For <i>Dawnguard</i>, it could be best to go with individuals or small groups.<br /> <br /> Harkon - He says he was a king who sacrifices a thousand souls to gain immortality directly from Molag Bal, the god who invented vampires. And he wants to blot out the sun. He's like one of the Ordo Dracul, but more arrogant and selfish. He doesn't care about mortals even as pawns. Neo-Tzimisce side of <b>Ventrue</b>? Probably could be any, although one thing he isn't is subtle.<br /> <br /> Valerica - She thinks Harkon's plan is stupid because it would turn everyone against them. As an accomplished necromancer, she's spent more centuries than she can count hiding in a dreary pocket realm full of lost souls. <b>Mekhet</b><br /> <br /> Serana - One thing that annoys fans is how the PC and Serana are friends from when they first meet whether you like it or not. THe PC activate contraption that push a spike though his hand and some blood gets siphoned to her coffin. You're sent by a group of vampire hunters and there's no option to kill her like the others. You just take her back to her castle (which means that the hunters could get to know where the vampires are based). Either she likes the PC or pretends to. She hasn't quite come to terms with her parents' indifference to her as a daughter. And the player doesn't really get resist her. <b>Daeva</b> much?<br /> <br /> The rest of Harkon's brood - Generally the men (as opposed to elves not women) like being able to rip arms off and the elves like magic and show a bit more decorum. Some of them scheme against each other and other find all that boring and/or immature. They stay in their castle away from the mortal world and mostly have their prey delivered to them. They do have a few operatives in the towns and conspire against hunters and other vampires, whom they see as vermin who make too much noise.<br /> <br /> <u>ESO</u><br /> I don't know, I haven't got that far yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T12:31:15-07:00","id":664644,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised that no one has mentioned &quot;A Girl Walks Home Alone At Night&quot; yet. It's set in a seedy ghost town in Iran, following a nameless girl who feeds on more mundane predators; drug dealers, pimps and the like. She coasts through the movie almost silently, just letting her victims project their usually exploitative motivations onto her. They lull themselves into a false sense of security through her lack of presence, and when she finishes with them, she takes some token(jewelery, a skateboard, a cat) from them. She is pretty much a perfect Mekhet. Watch it, you guys! I included the trailer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5WSMrSucjGA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5WSMrSucjGA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5WSMrSucjGA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5WSMrSucjGA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T14:40:01-07:00","id":664822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=664643#post664643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to try <i>Elder Scrolls</i> vampires.<br /> <br /> <u>Arena</u><br /> They're badarse spellcasters who wear cloaks. Not enough information<br /> <br /> <u>Daggerfall</u><br /> They look and sound weird, which would suggest <b>Nosferatu</b>, but nobody seems to notice that in game. In fact, one of them writes a book about his experiences and describes what it was like meeting a friend from life. He had been buried and everyone thought he was dead. Nobody recognised him, but he was treated much like a human stranger.<br /> There are nine &quot;tribes&quot;. All that distinguishes them is which cut cost spells they get. So I'll list them and make stuff up about them if needs be:<br /> <br /> Vraseth - &quot;Nimbleness&quot; - I think these guy as the types who scuttle around dungeons and trees and move unpredictably like Voldo from <i>Soul Calibur </i>or Jack from <i>Power Stone. </i>Apparently, the younger Queen Dowager thought that one of their castles would be a safe place to keep her private documents. That would fit a <b>Nosferatu</b> archetype nicely. That sort physical ability may otherwise match <b>Gangrel </b>or <b>Daeva</b>.<br /> <br /> Haarvenu - Big flashy fire and ice spells -These abilities wouldn't directly help them hunt, but they may be used to inspire awe and fear from mortal herds. I think of them setting up blood cults in rural western High Rock. <b>Daeva </b>or<b> Ventrue</b>?<br /> <br /> Garlythi - Shield - That's like fortitude so possibly <b>Gangrel </b>or<b> Ventrue</b>.<br /> <br /> Thrafey - Heal - A bit like the above. They're coded as enemies of the Anthosis. Perhaps they're a new tribe with a new ability so the Anthosis abduct them for study when they can. I'm going with <b>Gangrel</b>.<br /> <br /> Lyrezi - Silence and Invisibility - Probably <b>Mekhet</b>, but maybe <b>Nosferatu</b>.<br /> <br /> Khulari - Paralysis - Well certainly not Daeva. Could be <b>Mekhet, Nosferatu </b>or <b>Gangrel</b>.<br /> <br /> Montalion - Free action (cures paralysis) - The ability is worthless for two reasons and I've got nothing.<br /> <br /> Anthosis - They don't get a spell. They get a constant intelligence boost. I'd say <b>Mehket </b>or even <b>Jiang Shi</b><i>.</i><br /> <br /> Selenu - Resist fire, cold or shock. Better at withstanding the elements? How about <b>Gangrel</b>?<br /> <br /> <u>Morrowind</u><br /> As well as looking and sounding weird, everyone see that they're vampires in the mechanics, which means that you can hardly speak to anyone and everybody shouts at you or pleads for his life. They stay tombs and ruins. That's as <b>Nosferatu</b> as most vampires get in TES<i>. </i>There are three clans:<br /> <br /> Aundae - High Elves with enhanced willpower and magical ability. They also dress much more smartly than the other clans. They hypnotise their prey. <b>Ventrue</b>.<br /> Berne - Cyrodiils who pride themselves being able to go everywhere unseen. That's quite <b>Mekhet</b>.<br /> Quarra - Really strong Nords who run at their prey, grab and bite and probably spill a lot of the blood. Other clan think they're wasteful, ugly brutes and they think the other clans are pathetically weak, especially Aundae. <b>Gangrel</b><br /> <br /> <u>Oblivion</u><br /> They pass as mortals and rely on influence over mortal society. That's Invictus. I'd say <b>Ventrue</b>, based on the tone of their manifesto.<br /> <br /> <u>Skyrim</u><br /> Largely a rip off of <i>Oblvion's</i> vampires, but they can raise corpses and are more distant from mortal society. Some of them seem quite keen on eating flesh. For <i>Dawnguard</i>, it could be best to go with individuals or small groups.<br /> <br /> Harkon - He says he was a king who sacrifices a thousand souls to gain immortality directly from Molag Bal, the god who invented vampires. And he wants to blot out the sun. He's like one of the Ordo Dracul, but more arrogant and selfish. He doesn't care about mortals even as pawns. Neo-Tzimisce side of <b>Ventrue</b>? Probably could be any, although one thing he isn't is subtle.<br /> <br /> Valerica - She thinks Harkon's plan is stupid because it would turn everyone against them. As an accomplished necromancer, she's spent more centuries than she can count hiding in a dreary pocket realm full of lost souls. <b>Mekhet</b><br /> <br /> Serana - One thing that annoys fans is how the PC and Serana are friends from when they first meet whether you like it or not. THe PC activate contraption that push a spike though his hand and some blood gets siphoned to her coffin. You're sent by a group of vampire hunters and there's no option to kill her like the others. You just take her back to her castle (which means that the hunters could get to know where the vampires are based). Either she likes the PC or pretends to. She hasn't quite come to terms with her parents' indifference to her as a daughter. And the player doesn't really get resist her. <b>Daeva</b> much?<br /> <br /> The rest of Harkon's brood - Generally the men (as opposed to elves not women) like being able to rip arms off and the elves like magic and show a bit more decorum. Some of them scheme against each other and other find all that boring and/or immature. They stay in their castle away from the mortal world and mostly have their prey delivered to them. They do have a few operatives in the towns and conspire against hunters and other vampires, whom they see as vermin who make too much noise.<br /> <br /> <u>ESO</u><br /> I don't know, I haven't got that far yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wow, that is a lot, and games are an interesting take on the question. Thx.<br /> I just prefer not lock so much on specific characters, but more on the rough image of Vampires in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T14:41:34-07:00","id":664825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=664644#post664644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised that no one has mentioned &quot;A Girl Walks Home Alone At Night&quot; yet. It's set in a seedy ghost town in Iran, following a nameless girl who feeds on more mundane predators; drug dealers, pimps and the like. She coasts through the movie almost silently, just letting her victims project their usually exploitative motivations onto her. They lull themselves into a false sense of security through her lack of presence, and when she finishes with them, she takes some token(jewelery, a skateboard, a cat) from them. She is pretty much a perfect Mekhet. Watch it, you guys! I included the trailer.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5WSMrSucjGA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5WSMrSucjGA</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This one is obscure, even for me. But very interesting as well. thx","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T17:19:47-07:00","id":665071,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking over <i>Only Lovers Left Alive</i>:<br /> <br /> Both main characters seem like they'd fit into the Mekhet template, especially Eve; she's quick, and insightful, and loves collecting knowledge\u2014as exemplified by her massive library, packing books instead of clothes, and being able to 'read' them just by a touch. You could also argue Adam as being perhaps Nosferatu in a way, as he's more than a little spooky (especially when visiting the blood bank doctor, or driving away the people in the streets of Morocco with a simple glare and a &quot;You don't have what I need.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Eve's sister Eva, meanwhile? Daeva all the way. Impulsive, flighty, charming, but driven by her vices. As for Kit, it's tough to say, although erudite and refined as he is, and clinging as tightly as he does to his one companion (touchstone) Bilal, I'd vote on him being Ventrue.<br /> <br /> . . .<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, as for <i>What We Do in the Shadows</i> (seriously if you haven't seen this, you're missing out):<br /> <br /> Vladislav (the Poker!) with his temper problems and\u2014somewhat unskilled\u2014shapeshifting would probably be Gangrel. Nick would also have to qualify as such if you count shapeshifting and demeanor.<br /> <br /> Petyr is a Nosferatu, no question. The eldest and spookiest of the whole house.<br /> <br /> Viago would have to be Daeva. Foppish and seductive (but a bit, er, fastidious and more than a little clumsy).<br /> <br /> Deacon has to be a Ventrue. Arrogant, doesn't like to be told what to do (seriously, the chore wheel).<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;You will see nothing unusual!&quot; has to count as Dominate.<br /> <br /> Several other minor characters abound across the spectrum of archetypes, too. (Plus there are the zombies, the witches, and the s\u0336w\u0336e\u0336a\u0336r\u0336\u2014er, werewolves!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 09-23-2015, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T18:06:07-07:00","id":665109,"title":"","content":"If I were to draw parallels between the Warhammer fantasy bloodlines and the ones in NWOD it would probably go something like this. Of course the clans in nwod are fleshed out a bit more than their initial appearance so given more time I would probably change my mind but this is it at a glance.<br /> <br /> Von Carsteins - Ventrue : Lordly vampires that use their powers to dominate men and beasts to serve them. A good example of this is Vlad Von Carstein<br /> <br /> Lahmian - Deva : Manipulative socialites who get by on lies and charm. An somewhat more sympathetic example being Genevieve Dieudonne<br /> <br /> Necrarch - Mekhet/possibly Nosferatu : A bit more skeletal than your average Mekhet but personality wise they are quite similar being mystics with a love for darkness. Neborhest from Warhammer Online is basically the poster boy for these guys.<br /> <br /> Strigoi - Nosferatu: Monstrous, extremely violent and really not funny at all unless getting ripped to pieces by an undead monstrosity and its diseased ghoul servants is your idea of a good time. I can't think of any prominent members of the bloodline but I am sure you get the idea.<br /> <br /> Blood Dragons - Gangrel : Fighters who basically are locked in combat with their inner beast the founder managed to get himself some dragons blood and had somewhat of an ascension. Walach Harkon is a particularly badass member of this bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7683-thesummerian","user":"TheSummerian","date":". 09-14-2015, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7683-thesummerian","name":"TheSummerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T05:40:11-07:00","id":665569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=664644#post664644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised that no one has mentioned &quot;A Girl Walks Home Alone At Night&quot; yet. ... She is pretty much a perfect Mekhet. Watch it, you guys!</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur, on both counts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T21:04:45-07:00","id":666429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=657309#post657309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that Angel sired Drusilla, who sired Spike, so they'd all be the same Clan. I really think all three are Daeva.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant in terms of using them as inspiration. Oddly, someone in my group who did NOT watch Buffy, made a Malkavian who acted almost exactly like Drusilla, visions and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T21:24:28-07:00","id":666444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=664241#post664241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought the idea of <i>Underworld</i> stealing from the World of Darkness to be kind of silly. Most of the things that were complaints were things like, &quot;they sleep for a long time!&quot; and &quot;vampires and werewolves hate each other!&quot; Neither of which were particularly new even when the classic WoD was first published.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the biggest things was when someone called the idea of a hybrid an &quot;abomination&quot;. Very petty on WW's part.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T21:42:38-07:00","id":666460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=666444#post666444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the biggest things was when someone called the idea of a hybrid an &quot;abomination&quot;. Very petty on WW's part.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The plot of Underworld was pretty much lifted from a White Wolf story. And the way copyright works you need to defend it or later claims might be considered to have lost validity. 'You didn't say a word when Underworld was made, you can't suddenly sue Underworld 2: the Fall of the Sabbat.' Similar to how you could get stickers of Calvin pissing on everything because Bill Watterson was unaware of people doing it to begin with. To back up a claim you want to have as much evidence as possible, especially when you're talking about Sony Entertainment, which is far and beyond what White Wolf was. The fact is abomination is the term for werewolves turned vampires.<br /> <br /> So whether you think it's petty or not, it's practically required in order to retain the rights to the properties involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-16-2015, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T22:15:31-07:00","id":666468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=666460#post666460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The plot of Underworld was pretty much lifted from a White Wolf story. And the way copyright works you need to defend it or later claims might be considered to have lost validity. 'You didn't say a word when Underworld was made, you can't suddenly sue Underworld 2: the Fall of the Sabbat.' Similar to how you could get stickers of Calvin pissing on everything because Bill Watterson was unaware of people doing it to begin with. To back up a claim you want to have as much evidence as possible, especially when you're talking about Sony Entertainment, which is far and beyond what White Wolf was. The fact is abomination is the term for werewolves turned vampires.<br /> <br /> So whether you think it's petty or not, it's practically required in order to retain the rights to the properties involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the word abomination means &quot;object of hatred&quot;. It has nothing to do with vampires or werewolves, at least not specifically. If you hate broccoli, you could call broccoli an abomination. In Disney's &quot;Lilo and Stitch&quot;, Stich is called an abomination several times. The bad guy from the Incredible Hulk(Ed Norton) movie, Emil Blonsky, has been known to comic fans as THE Abomination since before the first edition of V:tM was even being written. Sorry, but WW was just wrong on that whole thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T00:02:47-07:00","id":666537,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm pretty sure the vamp/wolf hybrid in Underworld was called an &quot;abomination&quot;, not an &quot;Abomination&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T00:14:51-07:00","id":666543,"title":"","content":"The thing about them being called abominations was literally the least important part of Nofather's post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T19:52:04-07:00","id":672790,"title":"","content":"Most likely the vampires from Salem's Lot (novel version) are Ventrue given the heavy use of dominate but then Barlow was also shown to use what seemed like majesty at one point. For the vampires in Shiki I'm not sure since they showed obvious examples of dominate and vigor but some of them also showcased celerity while none of them really seemed to have any resilience. I wonder what D from Vampire Hunter D or most of the vampires in that show would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T19:58:31-07:00","id":672794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=672790#post672790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most likely the vampires from Salem's Lot (novel version) are Ventrue given the heavy use of dominate but then Barlow was also shown to use what seemed like majesty at one point. For the vampires in Shiki I'm not sure since they showed obvious examples of dominate and vigor but some of them also showcased celerity while none of them really seemed to have any resilience. I wonder what D from Vampire Hunter D or most of the vampires in that show would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't D a Dhampir?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T00:48:07-07:00","id":672978,"title":"","content":"Anybody got any ideas on vampires from the old Australian flick Thirst?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RfG8OKzFqQo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RfG8OKzFqQo\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RfG8OKzFqQo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RfG8OKzFqQo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What I like about them is that they walk in sunlight! Personally, I've long felt that the sunlight vulnerability was a modern idea (it started with Murnau's Nosferatu, I think) and isn't a necessary part of the vampire mythos. When I made my vampire comic in high school, the vampires there were nocturnal, but able to function during the day, too. And in the amazing Dracula by Coppola, Dracula is shown to walk the streets in daylight, too!<br /> <br /> Anyway! Anyone seen Thirst? Are the vampires there something specific?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T01:00:51-07:00","id":672984,"title":"","content":"Yes, he's a dhampyr (or &quot;Dunpeal&quot; if you watched the Bloodlust OAV), but he's treated more or less as a daylight-immune vampire than anything else. Honestly, even having watched both the OAVs and read a couple of the early novels, I'd be leery of translating them into WoD terms... they display traits of the Ventrue, some of the Daeva, with a big emphasis on Ordo Dracul mysticism and Invictus philosophy, with a few (like Carmilla) dabbling in Circle-esque blood sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T12:30:30-07:00","id":686052,"title":"","content":"Just saw \u201conly lovers left alive\u201d. Mekhet, no doubt!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T12:55:40-07:00","id":686062,"title":"","content":"The things in '<a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1336601/\" target=\"_blank\">La meute</a>' really struck me as nosferatu, though they had a feral, gangrel-like pack structure going on. No eyes, deformed jaws. Their origin story paralleled that of the Brothers Worm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T03:12:19-07:00","id":690998,"title":"","content":"Black Sabbath (or Vurdalak as you wish) - Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7277-brighella","name":"Brighella","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T23:08:30-07:00","id":703014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=486788#post486788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Get out of here with your not-mentioned-in-the-actual-show lore!<br /> <br /> (I am of course being playful and actually have nothing against the EU, I just loved the show, and everything I've heard about the comics and such has sounded very strange to me)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's very implied in the show, just not often. Kakistos (No, I did not verify the spelling :P ), the Master... They don't confirm it 100% but a lot of things the characters say implies strongly that over time, vampires become more and more demonic-looking. I think Whedon even confirms it in the first season commentary. (I wouldn't bet anything though, just going from memory.)<br /> <br /> P.S: Sorry if this was mentioned already, I'm still reading the thread but my geek side did not have the patience to wait for this reply! &gt;.&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8144-what_i_do_in_the_shadows","name":"What_I_Do_In_The_Shadows","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T23:17:28-07:00","id":703027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=488955#post488955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In comics, there was also an Elseworlds story where Batman faced Dracula, but not 'the' Dracula, and became a vampire. A particularly melodramatic one. But he was Gangrel all the way. In addition to showing signs of Animalism, through summoning and controlling bats, Protean, where he grew wings and shifted his body, as well as sank into the soil and turned into a dark mist. There was even Resilience.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i100.photobucket.com/albums/m27/victoria_wayne/c_arena/countdownarena_01_04.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>It WAS Dracula in 'Batman v.s Dracula: Red Rain'. Also, while I'd agree on Resilience anyway, the Vampire Batman stuff they did after the Moench/Jones trilogy of graphic novels was over (such as with the scanned example you gave) did not even fit with the original story's canon, so I always consider it as a different Earth's version that just happens to be extremely similar. For example, in one story they have that Batman acting evil and creating a vampire Robin. Except in 'Bloodstorm' he was still good, and in-between that one and Crimson Mist he was staked/in torpor, and then in Crimson Mist he never had time to 'fully' turn evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8144-what_i_do_in_the_shadows","user":"What_I_Do_In_The_Shadows","date":". 10-16-2015, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8144-what_i_do_in_the_shadows","name":"What_I_Do_In_The_Shadows","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T23:19:18-07:00","id":703028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan?p=657309#post657309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that Angel sired Drusilla, who sired Spike, so they'd all be the same Clan. I really think all three are Daeva.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I'd handle it is that vampires in the Buffyverse can 'choose' their Clans much like the rules for Bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8144-what_i_do_in_the_shadows","name":"What_I_Do_In_The_Shadows","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T08:11:22-07:00","id":703479,"title":"","content":"Looking at games, what about Nosgoth?<br /> (Yesyes, I know, it's nowhere what anyone wanted for a continuation of the Legacy of Kain, but you take what you can get.)<br /> Anyway, you have 5 Vampire classes as of now: Sentinel, Tyrant, Summoner, Deciever and Reaver. Since that stuff seems pretty<br /> muddy, why I think Class x is Clan X will be based on their skills and existing lore. Evolved skins remain ignored, since they only make matters harder/more inhuman.<br /> <br /> I'd say Summoners with all their necromantic magic (mostly just magic shields and necromantiv Hadouken) and calling on Ghost-thingies resemble Mekhet the most, based solely on Mekhet tendency to deal with the Dead. Other ideas that fit better?<br /> Decievers cloak themselves, turning invisible, deploy doubleg\u00e4nger images and can pretend to be specific humans. Which would be pretty much Nosferatu or Mekhet in my books. But they also<br /> have a sort of mindcontrol that deals damage rather similar to possession. Out of class-dominate? Since they hide their faces behind masks, we can't really say if they are or are not ugly. So a little unclear. Tending to Mekhet, again, since we have no signs of Vigor- average strength, no outstanding achievements there.<br /> Tyrants are durable and powerful, consider themselves nobility and act accordingly. Fits pretty well with Ventrue. Gangrel does not fit the spirit of their behaviour. Additional out-of-class Vigor since they can grab and throw humans single-handedly or dish out additional damage. I tend more towards Resilience-specced Ventrue though, since their tankiness is emphasised.<br /> Reavers are pretty obviously Daeva: Matrix-dodging multiple projectiles? Speed-buff? Passionate about their hunt? Check, check, double-check.<br /> Sentinel are the hardest to fit in somwhere for me, due to having wings, flying around and skills like sonar. According to Lore, they are basically starved and thus hardly more than animals.<br /> High-Level-Protean Gangrel very close with their Beast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T13:54:04-07:00","id":1123161,"title":"","content":"Am i the only one who sees Hannibal Lecter (NBC) as a possible Mekhet with Ordo Dracul Ties?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/